Well, I've seen no-MR ascensions, but I can't think that I've ever seen
a no-MC ascension...I'm sure it's possible, but it also seems like it'd
be very challenging.  Standard advice to players is to get *some* MC
asap, even if it's just putting on a mummy wrapping, since that cuts
the chances of being hit by certain potentially nasty attacks from 100%
to ~67%; MC2, which is fairly easy to get, drops that down to ~35%,
which is pretty safe.  Of course, MC1 is pretty easy to get, so
ascending without MC at all would require the player to make some tough
choices--no cloaks at all and only a limited subset of non-DSM body
armor would make the early game, especially, difficult.  Permanent
invisibility would be a good option, but only once you're 100% sure
you're done with the shops, since you'd have no way to make yourself
visible again (short of a "lucky" gremlin attack).  MR would have to
come from artifacts, and so is likely not an option until the
quest/castle.  Blessed genociding g, c, P, and V would help (I'm sure
there are others that could be added to the list--; for electric eels,
maybe?).  And some classes (orcish barbarians, monks, priests, rangers,
samurai, and wizards) would have to start by immediately stripping off
their armor/cloak, much as "zen" samurai must start by equipping their
blindfolds.  Dunno what other considerations one would have to make.

All that to say, the fact that MC2 ascensions are "easy and common"
doesn't show that MC is less important than MR; show us a no-MC
ascension, and then we can talk about whether it's easier to do than
no-MR.

